**Reader (who acts):** the objectui `domain:ui` lane.

## What is left

PR #13232 (`599a8a54bc`) added an enumeration ledger, `previews/flowNodeLabels.sites-13200.test.ts` (`ID_SITES`), which lists every flow-designer site that formats a node or edge name for display. It can only shrink. **13 entries are still open**: each still names a node by its id where the author gave it a label. All paths are under `packages/app-shell/src/views/metadata-admin/`:

1. `previews/FlowCanvas.tsx`: the edge tooltip `engine.flowCanvas.edge.undeclaredCycle` (source and target ids);
2. `previews/FlowCanvas.tsx`: the edge tooltip `engine.flowCanvas.edge.backEdge` (source and target ids);
3. `previews/FlowCanvas.tsx`: the plain edge tooltip, `source id → target id`;
4. `previews/FlowSimulatorPanel.tsx`: the simulator node list label (label, else id);
5. `previews/FlowSimulatorPanel.tsx`: the edge row fallback, `→ target id`;
6. `previews/flow-node-refs.ts`: the `where` of a reference site (holder id, or `source → target` ids);
7. `previews/flow-problems.ts`: `repeatedEdgeProblems`, `engine.flowProblems.repeatedEdge` (source and target ids);
8. `previews/simulator/flow-sim-validate.ts`: `engine.flowValidate.cycleDetected` (`cycle.join` of ids);
9. `previews/simulator/flow-sim-validate.ts`: `missingNodeRefDiagnostics`, `engine.flowValidate.boundaryHostMissing` (an existing boundary node by id);
10. `previews/simulator/flow-simulator.ts`: the `SimStep` label (label, else `nodeId`);
11. `inspectors/FlowNodeInspector.tsx`: the rename selection label (label, else the new id);
12. `inspectors/FlowNodeInspector.tsx`: the nested breadcrumb container crumb (container label, else id);
13. `inspectors/FlowNodeInspector.tsx`: the nested breadcrumb node crumb (label, else id).

**Expected:** each goes through the resolver `flowNodeDisplayName` / `flowEdgeDisplayName` (`previews/flow-canvas-parts.tsx`). Problems keep the id in parentheses, where labels can repeat, as objectui#13143 and #13200 ruled. The cycle message needs a shape: for example, labels joined by ` → `, with ids only where a label repeats. Each fixed site moves from open to resolver in `ID_SITES`, so the ledger ends with no open entries.

**Ruled exception, not in scope:** a node's own title beside its type eyebrow keeps "label, else id". These are recorded as `own-title` in `ID_SITES` (ruled B on objectui#13200).

